        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d834ec82-6e13-57c7-bb3d-13716f168c45",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Rynella, Iberia Parish, Louisiana, Highway 329, Avery Island\n- People: Rosemary McIlhenny, Pauline McIlhenny, Leila McIlhenny, Edward Avery McIlhenny\n- Companies: McIlhenny Company\n- Products: Tabasco sauce\n- Concepts: unincorporated communities, acronyms\n\nFacts:\n- Rynella is an unincorporated community in Iberia Parish, Louisiana, with a few residential dwellings and a volunteer fire department along Highway 329, also called the Avery Island Highway.\n- Rynella allegedly got its name from an acronym built from the last two letters of the first names of Rosemary, Pauline, and Leila McIlhenny, with an extra L later added.\n- Rosemary McIlhenny, Pauline McIlhenny, and Leila McIlhenny were daughters of Edward Avery McIlhenny.\n- Edward Avery McIlhenny was a noted Louisiana conservationist who presided over McIlhenny Company at nearby Avery Island.\n- McIlhenny Company makes Tabasco brand pepper sauce.\n- Tabasco sauce is a brand of hot sauce made exclusively from tabasco peppers, vinegar, and salt.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "68d49869-14ef-5a7f-954f-56610f4faa6e",
        "text": "Page: Rynella, Louisiana. Sentence: Rynella is an unincorporated community in Iberia Parish, Louisiana, that consists of a few residential dwellings and a volunteer fire department along Highway 329 (also known as the Avery Island Highway).\nPage: Rynella, Louisiana. Sentence: The name \"Rynella\" allegedly is an acronym deriving from the last two letters of the first names of three local women, Rosema\"RY\", Pauli\"NE\", and Lei\"LA\" McIlhenny (someone eventually adding an extra L to the resulting word).\nPage: Rynella, Louisiana. Sentence: They were daughters of Edward Avery McIlhenny, a noted Louisiana conservationist who presided over McIlhenny Company, maker of Tabasco brand pepper sauce at nearby Avery Island.\nPage: Tabasco sauce. Sentence: Tabasco sauce is a brand of hot sauce made exclusively from tabasco peppers (\"Capsicum frutescens\" var.\nPage: Tabasco sauce. Sentence: \"tabasco\"), vinegar, and salt.",
